'''''Ptychostomum schleicheri''''', the '''Schleicher's bryum moss''',<ref>{{Cite web|title=''Bryum schleicheri'' Schwägr.|url=https://www.itis.gov/servlet/SingleRpt/SingleRpt?search_topic=TSN&search_value=547640#null|url-status=live|access-date=25 January 2022|website=[[Integrated Taxonomic Information System]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220126002817/https://www.itis.gov/servlet/SingleRpt/SingleRpt?search_topic=TSN&search_value=547640 |archive-date=2022-01-26 }}</ref> is a species of [[moss]] belonging to the family [[Bryaceae]].<ref name="GBIF">{{cite web |title=Bryum schleicheri Schwaegrichen, 1816 |url=https://www.gbif.org/species/2676927 |website=www.gbif.org |access-date=13 February 2021 |language=en}}</ref> The leaves' color ranges from yellow to yellow-copper.<ref>{{eFloras|1|250099326|Ptychostomum schleicheri|first=John R. |last=Spence |access-date=15 July 2024}}</ref>

It is native to the [[Northern Hemisphere]].<ref name="GBIF" />

